<title>HUNGARY: CESI INDEX DROPS AS BUDAPEST, WARSAW, PRAGUE FALL.</title>
<headline>CESI INDEX DROPS AS BUDAPEST, WARSAW, PRAGUE FALL.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index fell on Thursday to close at 1,442.97 points, down 16.82 points or 1.15 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said on its Reuters page.</p>
<p>The index declined as all the three markets closed lower.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
